  "id": "delire-de-negation",
  "term": "délire de négation",
  "definition": "In this historical psychiatric term, a person in a delusional depressive state believes that they do not exist or are nobody, and may also believe that the world itself is unreal, destroyed, or gone. The source describes it as a marked form of depressive delirium appearing as an episode within melancholic states.",
